  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.render-test/the-printer-renders-each-nested-value-by-its-own-render seon.render-cost-test/render-calls-are-one-pass-over-their-nodes seon.render-cost-test/the-printer-renders-nested-values-in-one-pass seon.render-cost-test/main-info-reads-what-the-page-shows seon.context-test/an-owners-message-reaches-the-next-turn seon.context-test/a-taken-message-is-read-from-its-fact seon.agent-test/a-model-turn-records-its-prose-and-the-message-it-took seon.repl-test/a-forms-lead-is-recorded-with-its-eval seon.web-test/a-vector-headed-by-a-function-is-a-call seon.server-test/a-message-reaches-the-agent seon.model-test/cost-prices-a-turn-at-its-models-rates seon.render-test/a-units-change-rerenders-that-unit}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-agents-links-are-refs"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-23: \"keep the data in the database for easy pulling and rendering\"; a page is an entity and what one ref away (a-page-is-an-entity-and-its-neighbors needs this). What exists: the links between an agent, its run, its turns and its messages are names, not refs, so no pull follows them: :seon.run/agent is a keyword (:a3), :seon.turn/run and :seon.message/to are strings (the run's id), and :seon.agent/id :a3 is one identity for every boot's a3, so two boots' agents and their evaluations are one entity. Root (:seon.root/id) holds its agents only in its process's memory (its view), so its entity has no link to them; an agent's live state (pid, memory, the form running, its status) and the procs' numbers (the writer's batches, the fork server's forks) are not in the store at all. Correct: each link a ref (:db.type/ref): run -> agent, turn -> run, message -> run (and -> its sender), agent -> the root that started it; an agent entity per agent per boot (identity [boot id], the boot its root's :seon.root/boot); an agent's live state and each proc's numbers recorded as facts on its entity when they change, by their owner (root records an agent's status when its view changes; the writer its own numbers when it commits), never polled, no write on an idle system. No migration: the stored keys change with the run rename (jolt/rename-run), whose merge erases the store (DECISIONS). Deletes every string or keyword join between these entities (the d/q over :seon.turn/run, the message reader's lookup by :to, root's view as a second source of what an agent is)."
