 {:seon.task/name "data-is-cut-only-by-the-printer"
  :seon.task/plan "The owner's rule (2026-10-25, root's clipping audit, root's scratchpad clipping-audit.md): data is cut only by the one printer, at the end, when a value is printed into the model's context or a page; the full result is stored. What was cut before the printer, and what replaces it: (P1, P8) an eval's record stored the printed cut (:text, printed with the process's `seen`, so a record depended on the evals before it): `seon.repl/record-details` now keeps the response whole with its value when it is plain data (`seon.db/plain?`, stored once under its content key when large), else the response as it printed then (:printed) and the value's type; `seon.print/record-text` prints a record when it is sent or shown: the conversation prints each record once, when it is first sent, and reuses it by its id (`seon.context/printed-run`, per run in the agent's state; root's ruling 2026-10-25: a record's message is a function of it and the records before it), a value or output an earlier record showed folded to the form that reads it there, the fold named in its ref ([:eval id {:value result/e12}]) so the debug page reads back the same bytes (`seon.context/parts-of`); `seon.context/records` reads only the records since the last printed one; the page's eval view and root's outside and UI evals go through the same record-details. (P2) the last-evals path (`seon.context/evaluations-text`, the basis's :last-evals) and the dead `:seon.config.render/evals-budget` are deleted: each eval is its own message in the conversation. (P6, P7) `seon.render.ai`'s renders hand-formatted text with per-field cuts and bounded lists (`seon.print/bounded`, `more`, `:seon.config.render.list/{rows,brief,top}`): each render now makes a value (`task-data`, `run-data`, `error-data`, `problem-data`, `report-data`, `system-data`) printed once at the reader's budget, its cuts reading through the form that makes the value again; bounded, more and the three keys are deleted. `seon.repl`'s form echo is whole (its source, else its EDN). (P4) `seon.docs/resolve-ref` swapped a source over `:seon.config.render/reference-tokens` for its doc: the source is whole, the task data's printer cuts it, reading through `my.task/data`; the key is deleted. (P3) the history dropped whole records by an estimate: `seon.context/kept` now sends the newest whole, older ones whole while they fit, then collapsed (the result its handle and one line, the record's :line; ref [:line id]), the rest counted, both boundaries in steps of `:seon.config.render/history-step` (16) records so the prefix holds for many turns. (P5) `seon.context/similar`'s count stays: a retrieval count by config. Not covered (root's ruling, with the restart design): binding result/eN again after an agent restarts, from the stored value or its {:printed :type}; measured 0.74M ticks and 5.3 MB for 1,033 records on an in-memory db (one var per handle, the record scan 0.12M of it). Measured on the scripted run (fixtures/measure-replies, 7 turns): prompt tokens per turn 5,661..10,948 (58,914 total) before, 5,661..9,259 (55,533) after; turn 6's request 8.18M ticks / 32.6 MB cold, 3.62M / 14.3 MB with the run's printed records reused."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.context-test/a-record-keeps-its-value
                      seon.context-cost-test/a-turn-prints-its-new-records-flat-in-the-history
