 {:seon.task/name "a-walk-counts-its-rows-flat"
  :seon.task/plan "From the branch review of jolt/agent-conversation (2026-10-25, root's scratchpad branch-review.md, follow-ups): (F4) `seon.render/walk` with :limit pulls only the rows a page shows and lists the rest from the ref's index (no read of them): 59 contracted calls flat in the rows, but ~6 KB a row of bookkeeping (the index entry, the node map, the sort by transaction; seon.render-cost-test/a-page-walks-only-the-rows-shown, 3.24 / 8.65 MB at 100 / 1,000). Correct: the newest rows read by index from the end and their count read apart, so a walk costs the rows shown. Measure first: whether the eval entities' ids are in their transactions' order on every branch."
