 {:seon.task/name "a-page-is-its-components"
  :seon.task/plan "Render build 3 (docs/render.md, its refinement: a server-side ratom with the cursor inferred, and Datastar; the owner's go, 2026-10-26). What exists: an agent's page is its parts (seon.render/render-ctx as a vector of keyed parts, each drawn by part-faces into html through the :drawn memo, compared by hand-built keys: context/renders' task-key, cited-key, related-key, first-t), sent to root (seon.repl/parts), laid out by seon.render.ui/parts-page and diffed by html per unit in the render proc (step-units). The lab (shared notes render-investigation-2026-10-26.md, its ratom addenda) measured the replacement. Build: (1) seon.ratom, reagent.ratom ported with its names (RAtom, Reaction, run-in-reaction, flush!, dispose!) and a tracking view that infers the cursor, its hit test over seon.ctx/changes, the one diff; (2) the walk, in the agent where ctx lives: a component is a call [f opts & children] keyed by f and its children, its root element's id its key; a render whose opts declare :seon.ctx/ctx reads ctx through the view, one declaring :seon.db/db reads the db under d/with-reads; one cache (the component's reaction, args, db reads and output); a ledger of calls, hits, misses and allocation by the render's var; the view unwrapped where a value is drawn; (seon.render/page ctx) and (seon.render/page-diff p0 p1), [[op key hiccup]] with op :replace, :append (a keyed child new under a parent whose own output is otherwise unchanged) or :remove; (3) the agent page's layout as one component over ctx, its lists keyed by eid, the eval's handle anchor drawn by the eval's render, and the task render drawing from ctx what the task needs (each cited var's source, its deftests with source and last result, each cited section's text, the whole plan: the scratch paper context-for-20-turns-2026-10-26.md (git history) D1-D4) under cuts naming the form for the rest; (4) root's render proc sends an agent's frame (its page-diff, or its whole page for a keyframe) as Datastar events (seon.web/chunk-of), and draws an agent with no process by the same walk over its branch. Deletes render-ctx's parts, part-faces, part-html, drawn, context/renders' hand keys, seon.repl's :drawn memo, ui/parts-page and ui/agent-part, and step-units' compares for an agent page. Root's page and the debug page stay on the unit walk (every-page-is-its-parts). Follow-up, owned here: a plan edit costs 22.6M ticks on a3 (seon.reconcile/root-work-is-tasks), more than the worst change today, because task-data runs again whole and seon.docs/cited-view of its 8 cited sections is 4.6M of its 5.6M (about 580k a section; parsing the plan 0.46M, similar 0.17M, printing 0.58M); once ctx holds each cited section's text (ctx-atom's D3, its task pattern's :sections), task-data reads them from ctx and cited-view leaves the render. Owner: agent view."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.ratom-test/basic-ratom seon.ratom-test/test-unsubscribe seon.ratom-test/test-dispose seon.ratom-test/catching seon.ratom-test/inferred-paths seon.ratom-test/a-view-is-a-map
                      seon.render-test/a-component-re-runs-on-what-it-read seon.render-test/a-new-member-is-an-append seon.render-test/a-handle-links-to-its-eval seon.render-test/the-task-draws-what-it-needs
                      seon.render-cost-test/a-change-costs-its-components}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-status-before-any-model-turn"
  :seon.task/plan "Found building revision 4.2 (jolt/model-reads-the-page): the page's [:status] part (seon.render.ui/status over seon.context/turn-state) is drawn from the newest model turn's recorded basis (seon.render/render-ctx picks the run's :model turns), so an agent whose run has only an outside read (seon.turn/context-block, origin :outside), or none yet, shows no status: the person and an outside agent read no proofs, no done rule's reasons, no test run. What the outside read observed is recorded too (its turn's :seon.turn/basis :observed), so the fix is in render-ctx: draw [:status] from the newest turn of either origin, its turn count only for a model turn (turn-input already leaves it out for :outside). Before any turn at all, the part is absent, which is true: nothing observed yet. Proof: an agent page whose run has one outside read shows its proofs in [:status]."
